<task id="063" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-30 Record-scope MemoryItems via IComposeMemoryCapture facade (capture+recall; gate deferred)</title>
    <phase>6 Memory</phase>
    <gate>none</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>post-A0</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <dependencies>none — core durable store (IMemoryItemStore) + recall paths already shipped and on master</dependencies>
    <tags>bff-api, testing</tags>
    <fr>FR-30</fr>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Persist AI-derived Compose insights as durable, recallable `MemoryItem`s so a document's key knowledge
    (playbook deviations, defined-term canon, decisions) survives across sessions. Build the CAPABILITY now for
    dev/UAT via a new owner-blessed PublicContracts facade `IComposeMemoryCapture` that delegates to the EXISTING
    core durable store `IMemoryItemStore` (Cosmos `memory-items`) — the exact structural twin of the #615
    `IDocumentProfileAi` facade (delegate to a shared core primitive, no forked logic, ADR-013-clean). The
    untrusted-origin / memory-poisoning governance GATE (formerly AC3) is EXPLICITLY DEFERRED to the later
    system-wide memory-governance project (tracked by GitHub #629) — it is a governance-plane hardening layered
    ON TOP of this capture/recall stack, NOT a prerequisite for the capability. `TrustLevel` is carried on the
    envelope but left inert (unenforced) until that project, mirroring how the core `MemoryWriteHandler` already
    carries-but-does-not-enforce it.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer familiar with the AI facade seam (ADR-013), the core memory store (IMemoryItemStore /
    Cosmos `memory-items`), the #615 IDocumentProfileAi facade precedent, and create-on-save promotion in Sprk.Bff.Api.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Compose-derived insights persist as Record-scope `MemoryItem`s (keyed to the saved `sprk_document`) through a
    new `IComposeMemoryCapture` PublicContracts facade that delegates to `IMemoryItemStore.UpsertAsync`, carrying
    the full provenance envelope (tenant, scope, provenance{bindingId, ledgerRef}, trustLevel carried-but-inert).
    A through-the-wire CAPTURE→RECALL test proves an insight written by the facade is readable back via the store,
    the `GET /api/memory/records/{entity}/{id}` endpoint, AND lands in the chat Record prompt fragment. No local
    MemoryItem variant is introduced. The untrusted-origin gate is deferred (documented, tracked by #629).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Investigation (2026-07-15, #629 re-triage) established there is NO technical blocker to the capture/recall
      CAPABILITY — only the poisoning gate is missing, and that is the owner's separate later governance project.
      Grounded facts: (a) the durable store `IMemoryItemStore` → Cosmos `memory-items` container already exists,
      is registered in `AiPersistenceModule` (NOT behind the compound-AI gate), and exposes
      `UpsertAsync(MemoryItem, tenantId, ct)` decoupled from any chat context; (b) recall already works —
      `GetForRecordAsync`, `ToRecordPromptFragmentAsync`, and `GET /api/memory/records/{entityLogicalName}/{id}`
      (MemoryGovernanceEndpoints) have no chat-only guard; (c) the core `MemoryWriteHandler`'s
      `SupportedInvocationContexts => Chat` guard is an UNIMPLEMENTED-PATH guard, not the governance gate — the
      gate lives in `ConfirmationPolicyEngine`/`SideEffectGateAIFunction`. So the #615 facade pattern applies
      directly: a new facade injects the same `IMemoryItemStore` the chat handler uses and upserts a Record-scope
      MemoryItem. Scope-mapping was already resolved in HANDOFF-to-core-fr30-anchor-2026-07-12.md: anchor to the
      `sprk_document` (Record scope), promoted at create-on-save, hook point
      `ComposeService.SaveAsync → PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` (ComposeService.cs:362-371).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/IMemoryItemStore.cs" role="reference">The shared durable store the facade delegates to — UpsertAsync (persist), GetForRecordAsync (recall). Do NOT reimplement; inject and call.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Memory/MemoryItemStore.cs" role="reference">Cosmos-backed impl; deterministic id over (scope,factType,key) → upsert-by-key supersession. Enforces its own invariants (subject keying, DataverseFieldMirrorGuard).</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/MemoryWriteHandler.cs" role="reference">The envelope-construction reference (:288-311) — mirror the provenance/TrustLevel-carried-inert shape exactly. Do NOT route through this handler; it is chat-only.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IDocumentProfileAi.cs" role="reference">The #615 facade PRECEDENT to mirror in structure, ownership framing, best-effort/never-throw posture, and DI registration.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IComposeMemoryCapture.cs" role="create">NEW facade interface — owner-blessed canonical PublicContracts contract (same framing as IDocumentProfileAi).</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ComposeMemoryCapture.cs" role="create">NEW impl — injects IMemoryItemStore, builds Record-scope MemoryItem, UpsertAsync; best-effort/never-throw.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs" role="edit">Inject ONLY IComposeMemoryCapture (optional ctor param, ADR-032 null-tolerant). Wire insight capture at SaveAsync → PromoteIfEphemeralAsync (:362-371).</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AiPersistenceModule.cs" role="edit">Register the facade near IMemoryItemStore (or in the compound-AI gate if LLM distillation is involved).</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Memory/MemoryGovernanceEndpoints.cs" role="reference">GET /api/memory/records/{entity}/{id} — the recall endpoint the E2E test reads back through.</file>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/HANDOFF-to-core-fr30-anchor-2026-07-12.md" role="contract">Resolved scope-mapping + anchor/hook point.</file>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md" role="spec">§8 derivedInsights disposition + deviation note.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="ready">Core durable store + recall paths are already on master. No core dependency remains for the capability.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Memory tiers: insights are Record-scope (Cosmos Tier-3), governed, carry retention/expiration semantics per the memory model.</constraint>
    <constraint source="charter-3.4">NO local MemoryItem variant — build the facade against the published `MemoryItem` contract and the existing `IMemoryItemStore`; add no Compose-owned memory type or store.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">`Services/Compose/` injects ONLY the `IComposeMemoryCapture` PublicContracts facade — never `IMemoryItemStore`, `IOpenAiClient`, memory internals, or the chat handler directly (Tier-1 NetArchTest must stay green). The facade impl lives under `Services/Ai/` and may depend on the store.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Provenance on each MemoryItem references the ledger (`bindingId` / `ledgerRef` = `{bindingId}@t{n}`), never a duplicated payload.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope-decision-2026-07-15">Untrusted-origin / memory-poisoning GATE is DEFERRED (owner decision): capability now in dev/UAT, governance plane in a separate later project (#629). Carry `TrustLevel` on the envelope but DO NOT enforce it here. Document the deferral inline + in the facade header, referencing #629.</constraint>
    <constraint source="best-effort">Capture NEVER throws to the caller (mirror IDocumentProfileAi) — a failed insight-capture must never fail or block a document Save.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the #615 `IDocumentProfileAi` facade + `IMemoryItemStore` + `MemoryWriteHandler` envelope construction. Confirm the store's `UpsertAsync` signature + the `MemoryItem` fields (scope, subjectType/subjectId, factType, key, value, provenance, trustLevel, expiration).</step>
    <step order="2">Author `IComposeMemoryCapture` + `ComposeMemoryCapture`: build a Record-scope `MemoryItem` keyed to the resulting `sprk_document` (subjectType="sprk_document", subjectId=documentId), set the provenance envelope exactly as MemoryWriteHandler does (Source=AiDerived, bindingId, ledgerRef, sessionId, tenantId), carry `TrustLevel` inert, and call `store.UpsertAsync`. Best-effort/never-throw + logged. Canonical owner-blessed header framing (mirror #615), with the #629 gate-deferral note.</step>
    <step order="3">Distill genuinely-durable insights (playbook deviations, defined-term canon, decisions) from the dispatched-action outputs — NOT raw action payloads. Map each to one MemoryItem (factType + stable key for upsert-by-key supersession).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire into `ComposeService.SaveAsync → PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` (:362-371): inject the facade as an optional null-tolerant ctor param (ADR-032); capture insights for the promoted `sprk_document`. Do not block or fail Save on capture error.</step>
    <step order="5">Register the facade in `AiPersistenceModule` (near `IMemoryItemStore`, or in the compound-AI gate if distillation is LLM-driven, mirroring `DocumentProfileAi`).</step>
    <step order="6">CAPTURE→RECALL E2E slice test (compose E2E DoD): facade write → assert readable via `store.GetForRecordAsync`, via `GET /api/memory/records/sprk_document/{id}` (WebApplicationFactory through the real route), AND present in `ToRecordPromptFragmentAsync`. Plus unit tests: envelope fully populated; no-local-variant; capture-never-throws-on-store-failure.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify build + Tier-1 NetArchTest facade rule green; report publish-size delta (BFF hygiene §10).</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Overlaps with the core Memory subsystem (`IMemoryItemStore`, `MemoryItem`). Verified: the store + recall already exist and are decoupled from chat; Compose adds NO store and NO MemoryItem subtype — only a thin PublicContracts facade (ADR-013 requirement for CRUD→memory access).</existing>
    <extension>Extends the core memory model by CONSUMING `IMemoryItemStore` through a facade — the exact #615 pattern. No new store, no MemoryItem variant, no forked persistence logic.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without durable capture, AI-derived Compose insights vanish between sessions (no continuity) — the core FR-30 user value (a document "remembers" its playbook deviations / defined-term canon / decisions) is inert despite the store existing.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IComposeMemoryCapture.cs (new)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ComposeMemoryCapture.cs (new)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — wire capture at PromoteIfEphemeralAsync</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AiPersistenceModule.cs — facade registration</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ComposeMemoryCaptureTests.cs (facade unit)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/.../ComposeMemoryCaptureRecallTests.cs (CAPTURE→RECALL through the wire)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Compose insights persist as Record-scope `MemoryItem`s (keyed to the saved `sprk_document`) via `IComposeMemoryCapture` → `IMemoryItemStore.UpsertAsync`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each write carries the full provenance envelope: tenant, scope=Record, provenance{bindingId, ledgerRef}, trustLevel (carried, inert), expiration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CAPTURE→RECALL proven through the wire: a captured insight is readable via `store.GetForRecordAsync`, via `GET /api/memory/records/sprk_document/{id}`, AND appears in the chat Record prompt fragment.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No local MemoryItem variant is introduced; the existing `MemoryItem` contract + `IMemoryItemStore` are consumed as-is.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Capture never throws to the caller — a store failure does not fail or block a document Save (test-verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects only the facade; BFF build + Tier-1 NetArchTest facade rule green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false" deferred="true" tracked-by="#629">DEFERRED to the later memory-governance project: untrusted-origin gate / TrustLevel ENFORCEMENT / poisoning evals. NOT built here (owner decision 2026-07-15). Documented inline + in the facade header.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the `MemoryItem` contract or `IMemoryItemStore.UpsertAsync` shape differs materially from what this task assumes (e.g., no Record-scope subject keying, or UpsertAsync requires a chat context), STOP and report — do NOT fork a local MemoryItem variant (charter §3.4). Re-confirm the store shape before proceeding.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
